{"claims":[{"claim_text":"Michael Harrington likely did not set out to create a party of professional reformists, but a former staffer sympathetic to membership affirms Red Star’s view that this is the modus operandi of the social-democratic wing of the organization and their aligned staffers.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Members are thought to be too unreliable and transient to do the political work of planning and directing strategic campaigns, and this crucial political work should be left to paid staffers.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"The vast majority of the membership are relegated to the grunt work of canvassing, phone banking, text banking, and bankrolling the organization through dues.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This vision for DSA does not value members as thinkers, organizers, leaders, or decision makers.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Red Star views the organizational mode as a failure.", "claim_types":["evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA has not persuaded non-socialist legislators to back reforms like Medicare for All, the Green New Deal, and the PRO Act.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Losing the Bowman and Bush seats shows there is no clear path to a socialist legislative supermajority.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"In the post-2016 era, DSA’s strength and success has come primarily from the organizing work of its locals.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA has flourished not as a vehicle for national reform campaigns, but as a laboratory where socialists have learned and grown through organizing experience and dialogue with one another.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
```

